{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "colored sprites s + red marker pixels",
  "transform": "mirror s across the red marker axis (vertical/horizontal red line) or point-reflect around an isolated red pixel; paint the mirrored pixels onto bg"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 18-28 rows × 18-28 cols
  background: any single color (most frequent), dominates grid
  marker_color: always red (2)
  marker_groups: 3-7 per grid, each is one of three types
  type_1_row:
    structure: horizontal red line (≥2 px, all share one row) 4-connected to a monochromatic payload sprite on one side
    red_length: 2-6
    payload: 3-11 px of a single non-red non-bg color, entirely above or below the red row
    transform: mirror payload across the red row; paint mirrored px onto bg
  type_2_col:
    structure: vertical red line (≥2 px, all share one column) 4-connected to a monochromatic payload sprite on one side
    red_length: 2-6
    payload: 3-11 px of a single non-red non-bg color, entirely left or right of the red column
    transform: mirror payload across the red column; paint mirrored px onto bg
  type_3_isolated:
    structure: single red pixel with NO 4-connected non-bg neighbors; exactly 1 adjacent (8-conn) non-bg non-red color component
    transform: point-reflect that entire 8-connected color component around the red pixel; paint mirrored px onto bg
    adjacent_sprite: 1-8 px [observed]
  payload_colors: each payload/sprite uses exactly one non-red non-bg color; distinct colors per group [observed]
  spatial: all sprites + mirrored copies must fit within grid; no overlap between mirrored pixels and existing non-bg pixels
  non_participating_sprites: 0-8 free single-px or small sprites that share a payload color, located near enough to be caught by bbox-based eligibility in solver

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first — build mirrored output, then remove mirrored pixels to derive input
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size H×W ∈ [18,28], bg color (not 2)
    2. Decide marker count (3-7) and type mix (row, col, isolated)
    3. For each row/col marker — build the full mirrored output sprite pair first
       a. Pick payload color (non-bg, non-2, unique per group)
       b. Generate random connected payload sprite (3-11 px)
       c. Place red line adjacent to one edge; mirror payload across line
       d. Place assembled group (payload + reds + mirror) on empty canvas region
    4. For each isolated marker — build sprite + point-reflected copy
       a. Pick a color; generate small 8-connected sprite (1-8 px)
       b. Choose red pixel location 8-adjacent to one sprite pixel
       c. Point-reflect entire sprite around red; place all on canvas
    5. Optionally scatter 0-3 free single-pixel sprites of same payload colors near marker groups
    6. Derive input by erasing all mirrored pixels (keeping originals + reds)
    7. Oracle: main(input) == output
```
